Ladybird resolves a unitless line-height to the number times the
computed font size, in pixels, whether or not the element has a box.
Blink’s ComputedStyleUtils::ValueForLineHeight() does the same from
the style alone, and so does WebKit’s LineHeight extractor, which
multiplies the number by the used font size for every value type but
the computed one. Firefox returns pixels for unrendered elements too.
